{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The New Waiter", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Cultural Differences", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's backgrounds in a wider variety  of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are common, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Inseparable phrasal verbs are very common. The verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed<br/>    <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.</span></li> <li>take off = leave the ground  <br/>         The plane took off on time.</span></li> <li>look out = beware! be careful!   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the following inseparable phrasal verbs to describe life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to sit down\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to sit properly on a chair\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to dig in\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to start eating\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to hold on to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to keep something dearly\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to pass on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to place into the custody of someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to dress down\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to dress very casually\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "We all sit down with our families and enjoy our meal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've also noticed that people don't mind dressing down for work or for going out.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Should and Be Supposed To ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modal  <span class=\"strong\">should</span> or the  structure  <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use  <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the present or future that are expected to happen. <br/><br/> The structure is:<br/><br/>  Subject + To be + supposed to + verb<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Sharing information with their new colleagues is something they're <span class=\"strong\">supposed to do</span> .</span> <br/><br/>  **Pronunciation tip**:<br/> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br/><br/> Like this:<br/> Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You're supposed to wear something nice if you're going to be seen in public. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Men and women should always be well-dressed.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to sit down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to sit properly at a table for a meal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We all sit down with our families and enjoy our meal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about culture and tradition.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to dig in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to start eating", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The food is getting cold. Dig in!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hold on to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to keep something dearly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In my country, people hold on to their traditions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "decorum", "type": "name"}, {"content": "good behaviour, good etiquette and good taste", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Decorum? That's when everything is supposed to be done according to the rules. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pass on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give someone something that someone else has given you", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Appreciating a good meal is definitely something we should pass on to the future generations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to dress down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to wear informal clothes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've noticed that people don't mind dressing down for work or for going out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "two left feet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "clumsy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't dance very well because I have two left feet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Your friend is visiting our city.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Brainstorm 8-10 pieces of advice you could give your friend about customs and manners here in this country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use supposed to/ not supposed to.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare with a partner and make a list of the top 5 most important points.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner make a poster including pictures representing your top 5 points.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present it to the class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about manners and customs. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about things that I'm supposed to do and things that are  supposed to happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present information in an interesting manner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about manners and customs. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about life experiences. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that I'm supposed to do and things that are  supposed to happen.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What traditions do you 